00:00:54.530 --> 00:01:00.309
Question 1 - Lukas asks will we see a civil
war in the earth kingdom (people against the

00:01:00.309 --> 00:01:01.969
queen)?

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:08.350
Usually there are multiple conflicts that
either overlap or go happen at the same time

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:14.970
during the finale. Like Korra will have her
battle with the Team Zaheer plot and there

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.250
will be some sort of human versus human conflict.

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:24.320
Based on what we've seen so far, I don't see
anyone else becoming the villain of that human

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.240
conflict. So yes to the Earth Queen versus
her people. I don't know if it will just turn

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:32.229
out to be a straight up civil war, but no
one will be killing anyone. That's not really

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:36.619
what Korra is about and it wouldn't fit with
the Airbending philosophy that all life is

00:01:36.619 --> 00:01:36.909
sacred.

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:40.670
The Earth Queen was subjigating all her citizens
yes, not just Airbenders, but I think it would

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:47.670
be really cool if we saw those Earth Kingdom
airbenders return to Ba Sing Se to help make

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:49.200
peace.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.310
The Earth Queen is a lot like the Queen of
Hearts from Alice in Wonderland. Really over

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.890
the top crazy and comical. But I think there
are a couple ways her plot could resolve itself.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:01.590
One would be for Korra and the Airbenders
to teach her the error of her ways, or some

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:08.590
of her power could be taken away and the Earth
Kingdom could appoint a parliment. Like what

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:15.910
happened in the UK. The monarchy still exists,
but over the last 100 years, the royal family

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.489
has slowly given more and more of their decision
making power to the government.

00:02:19.489 --> 00:02:24.700
To the point where Queen Elizabeth is more
of a figurehead and Parliment does the day

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:30.069
to day job of making sure species 456 doesn't
kill everyone. Shout out to all the torchwood

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:31.150
fans.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:36.819
Question 2 - Camile asks what was so important
about Korra that Team Zaheer couldn't do it

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:38.660
with Aang when he was still alive?

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.690
Good question, so Korra is almost 19 right
now. So let's assume Team Zaheer was put in

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.980
prison the year she was born. They look like
they're about the same age as Tenzin, so they

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.400
would have been in their early 30s when they
were arrested.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:56.400
I can think of two big reasons why they'd
go for Korra versus Aang. The first is that

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.209
Aang was dying by the time they put their
plan together. Like Aang was in his final

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:04.739
years and either wouldn't have had enough
strength to do whatever Zaheer wanted the

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:09.650
avatar to do OR if they're just trying to
convince the avatar to help them, Aang was

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.170
too stuck in his ways and would have never
agreed to their mystery plan.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:21.170
I think it's a combination of those two things.
They saw Aang was on his way out, so they

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.920
thought it would be easier to raise a new
avatar teaching her their philosophy, so Korra

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.519
would make things the way they wanted.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:36.690
That's kind of a twist on what Unalaq wanted,
except he wanted to kill Raava. I don't think

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:40.470
that's what Zaheer wants. There's still too
much we don't know about him to guess what

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:40.739
his plan is.

00:03:40.739 --> 00:03:45.799
I'm just going to call it his mystery plan
until Zaheer does an evil guy monologue explaining

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:46.900
it all.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.580
Question 3 - Wargaming (no avatar) asks Where
did Zuko's Dragon come from?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:54.220
In the Dragon Days comic, Aang saves the last
Dragon egg. I'm assuming it's either the dragon

00:03:54.220 --> 00:04:01.220
that hatched from that Egg. During Last Airbender
they learned Iroh had protected Ran and Shaw

00:04:01.629 --> 00:04:02.830
too.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:08.760
We learned in that Zuko video game Nickelodeon
released on their website that his dragon's

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:15.030
name is Druk. He was born around 18 years
ago. Meaning it's about the same age as Korra.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:18.769
It's funny to think that the birth of Zuko's
Dragon and the birth of a new Avatar are connected.

00:04:18.769 --> 00:04:23.470
But I can see why they would connect those
two big events. I'm sure there are a lot of

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:28.050
big things that were connected to Korra's
birth. Including Zaheer's mystery plot.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:33.220
The takeaway is that Druk is probably the
progeny of the dragons from last airbender

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:38.800
or his egg was laid when Firelord Sozin was
killing them all and just survived to hatch

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.620
when Korra was born.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:44.750
I've always thought that dragon eggs take
forever to hatch, just because in all the

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:51.750
different fantasy series I've ever seen. Dragons
are an extremely long-lived race.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:01.960
Question 4 - Benjamin asks Do you think Aang
was the one that taught Zaheer about Airbending?

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.979
Yes it's definitely possible. I saw a lot
of you guys speculating that Zaheer was an

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:12.979
early air disciple when Tenzin was growing
up and learned about something dangerous and

00:05:13.199 --> 00:05:20.199
tried to do something crazy. Aang took his
bending away and then years later when Zaheer

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.860
tried to kidnap Korra they were all locked
away.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:30.860
Making this like his third try to do whatever
he's trying to do. And Harmonic Convergence

00:05:31.169 --> 00:05:34.840
restored his bending that Aang took away.
It would explain why he's so good. And there

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.130
wouldn't have been many people other than
aang who could have taught him about airbending

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.090
30 or forty years ago.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:50.090
Question 5 - Andre asks do you think Opals
actually Lin's daughter?

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:59.229
No, I don't think it's going to be that complicated.
I think that the whole Lin Suyin backstory

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:04.110
is going to be a simple take on their big
differences. Like Beifong trying to be super

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:08.550
responsible and strict and Suyin being rebellious
and getting away with everything.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:15.550
Suyin said that Toph wasn't super proud of
either one of them in the end, but Lin is

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:23.380
probably just bitter about Suyin never being
held to account for her actions.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:31.850
That explanation makes Lin seem like more
of an emotional child in that she can't just

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:36.440
get over the fact they see the world differently.
But I think we're meant to draw some similarities

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:41.270
in the way Lin and the Earth Queen are both
behaving ridiculously and need to open their

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:41.550
eyes.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:45.190
Lin is a good person, so I think she'll get
there eventually.

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:50.600
Question 6 - Kevin (no avatar) asks Maybe
the real antagonists are the White Lotus?

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:57.600
I think the real antagonist is ignorance.
Like all the characters will have to get used

00:06:58.669 --> 00:07:02.740
to change and that's the real obstacle to
overcome. Zaheer just seems like the villain

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.530
right now because his plan takes him in opposition
to Team Avatar.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:10.360
The White Lotus people we've seen so far this
season haven't done anything that make the

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:13.069
villains. They're really just following Zuko's
orders at this point and Zuko isn't the villain.

00:07:13.069 --> 00:07:17.139
It sounds silly but they'll all probably get
to the point this season when a real change

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:21.080
will come and everyone in the world will just
have to learn to deal. It kind of already

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.669
happened with Harmonic Convergence. But Zaheer
could always be trying to bond the physical

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:27.069
realm with the spirit realm in a much bigger
way.

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:32.610
That spirit Korra almost hit in Republic City
said we're all the same, even the avatar should

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:37.889
know that. It just sounds very ominous to
me, like everyone really will become the same

00:07:37.889 --> 00:07:40.039
in a much more obvious way.

00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:44.970
Question 7 - Chivaugh asks Is it just me or
has the Dai Li and White Lotus gotten less

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:45.449
badass?

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:52.449
I think they just want to make the new characters,
Kai and Team Zaheer, seem like bigger badasses.

00:07:53.379 --> 00:07:57.979
They're more of a threat if they can take
down the White Lotus and the Dai Li.

00:07:57.979 --> 00:08:03.560
And since the world hasn't really been at
war in a huge global way since Aang's time,

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:07.620
people might have gone a little soft. So the
Dai Li and the White Lotus could both be more

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:12.009
like maintenance level benders, not the kind
of superhero epic benders you see emerge during

00:08:12.009 --> 00:08:19.009
times 
of war.

00:08:21.639 --> 00:08:25.389
Question 8 - Danny Phantom asks Do you think
Zaheer's Void has something to do with the

00:08:25.389 --> 00:08:26.569
original Airbenders?

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:32.180
Not necessarily, but I do think it has to
do with energy bending and transcending physical

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.750
existence. I know I mentioned conquering death
in my last video, but the best way to do that

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:41.519
would be to exist as pure energy. That might
not be what Zaheer is trying to do exactly.

00:08:41.519 --> 00:08:44.390
But I don't think he's just trying to contact
someone.

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:50.480
I think he's trying to energy bend everyone
or some twist on the astral state we've seen

00:08:50.480 --> 00:08:56.390
Korra and Aang go into when they get super
Zen. Guru Pathik's Chakra's might get referenced

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:56.890
again.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:09:02.769
Question 9 - iloveme asks Why did Nick take
all the episodes down off Nick.com?

00:09:02.769 --> 00:09:08.019
Probably because they want to try to increase
live ratings for Korra. I don't think it will

00:09:08.019 --> 00:09:11.600
work and I don't think that their strategy
of not putting episodes on itunes quickly

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.720
is going to work either. Right now the only
way to watch the show legally is to watch

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:20.200
it on Nickelodeon. But if you live in a country
where Nick isn't available which is most places.

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.250
It really hurts their viewership.

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:26.930
It's a whole big thing. So my sympathies to
anyone who's having trouble watching new episodes.

00:09:26.930 --> 00:09:31.140
I can't allow any streaming links in the comments
here, just because they are illegal, but that's

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:36.750
